  "text": "The home mountain of the Greek Gods is Mount Olympus.\n\nTo understand how search engines work, imagine the Internet as a massive library. In this analogy, websites are like entire books, and individual web pages are the specific pages within those books. Just as a library index helps you locate the exact book and page you need, search engines like Google act as that index, helping you find the specific website and page containing the information you are looking for."
